$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 8-chloro-2-(thiophen-2-ylsulfanyl)quinoline (2). A solution
1.00g (.005mol) 2,8-dichloroquinoline and .70g(.006mol) 2-thiophenethiol
was stirred and heated at 75°C for 10min. After cooling, the mixture was
diluted with 20mL ethyl acetate. The organic layer was washed three times
with equal portions of 5% sodium sulfite, then once with an equal portion
of 10% sodium hydroxide, dried with magnesium sulfate and allowed to
evaporate. 1.00g of solid 2 were obtained which required no further
purification (72% yield). mp: semi solid at room temp. 1H NMR (400MHz,
CDCl3) 7.94 (d, 1H), 7.78 (d, 1H), 7.65 (m, 2H), 7.45 (d, 1H), 7.35 (t,
1H), 7.20 (m, 1H), 7.08 (d, 1H). 13C NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) 119.2, 126.5,
127.0, 127.6, 127.6, 127.7, 128.9, 129.5, 130.5, 137.5, 137.6, 144.3,
164.3. IR (NaCl) 3400, 3000, 1100, 903. Anal. calc. 276.97 m/z ASAP (-
mode) 275.97 (C13H8ClNS2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalyst-Free Preparation of Heterocyclic Thienyl Sulfides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Barrett, Kristen; McKee, James; Zanger, Murray
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2015), 45(24), 2857-2860

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME43 STEP1
