$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for synthesis of aryl
thiocyanates 2 A Schlenk tube was charged with diaryliodonium salts 1
(0.5 mmol) and KSCN (2.0 mmol, 4.0 equiv) dissolved in DCE (5 mL) in an
air atmosphere. The mixture was stirred vigorously at rt for 5 min. Then,
the reaction was stirred at 80°C and monitored by thin-layer
chromatography (TLC) until 1 was consumed completely (18-24 h). At this
time, the DCE was removed under reduced pressure and the crude product
was purified by flash chromatography (dry loading with SiO2) using
eluents (1:50 ethyl acetate/petroleum ether to 10:1) to provide product 2
as oil or solid. Thiocyanatobenzene (2a)[5g] 4-Thiocyanatobiphenyl
(2j),[4] white solid, 73.8 mg, 70% yield. Mp: 89-90°C; 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.64 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.59-7.55 (m, 4H), 7.47 (t, J = 6.5
Hz, 2H), 7.40-7.37 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ 142.8, 139.3,
130.6, 129.0, 128.8, 128.2, 127.1, 122.9, 110.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Transition-metal-free synthesis of thiocyanato- or nitro-arenes through
diaryliodonium salts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Xiao-Hua; Li, Liang-Gui; Mo, Xue-Ling; Mo, Dong-Liang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2016), 46(11), 963-970

